e form $ax=b.$ \n\nWe start by subtracting $5x$ from both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7px & =5x+9 \\\\ 7px-5x & =5x+9-5x \\\\ 7px-5x & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we factor $x$ on the left-hand side. This gives\n\n$$\n(7p-5)x=9.\n$$\n\nNotice that this equation is now in the form $ax=b:$\n\n$$\n{{(7p-5)}_{⏟}}_{a}x={{9}_{⏟}}_{b}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n7p-5=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7p-5 & =0 \\\\ 7p-5+5 & =0+5 \\\\ 7p & =5 \\\\ \\frac{7p}{7} & =\\frac{5}{7} \\\\ p & =\\frac{5}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["6bd3e1cf-0ff1-5b2d-b46d-e9dc96d139b2"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "ddee9766-6222-5ace-b4c6-519ec6c434e0" :answer/id #uuid "ddee9766-6222-5ace-b4c6-519ec6c434e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "fb8540a4-f01f-56fa-9999-4f7e33a5d3ea" :answer-field/id #uuid "fb8540a4-f01f-56fa-9999-4f7e33a5d3ea" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/choices ["ddee9766-6222-5ace-b4c6-519ec6c434e0"] :answer-field/correct "ddee9766-6222-5ace-b4c6-519ec6c434e0" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "d7b7776b-e31d-5294-a559-386b1ec0c77e" :question/id #uuid "d7b7776b-e31d-5294-a559-386b1ec0c77e" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $u,$ given by\n\n$$\n4qu+4=9u-8\n$$\n\nwhere $q$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $q?$\n\n$q=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the equation in the form $au=b.$ \n\nWe start by subtracting $9u$ from both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4qu+4 & =9u-8 \\\\ 4qu-9u+4 & =9u-8-9u \\\\ 4qu-9u+4 & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we subtract $4$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4qu-9u+4 & =-8 \\\\ 4qu-9u+4-4 & =-8-4 \\\\ 4qu-9u & =-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we factor $u$ on the left-hand side. This gives\n\n$$\n(4q-9)u=-12.\n$$\n\nNotice that this equation is now in the form $au=b:$\n\n$$\n{{(4q-9)}_{⏟}}_{a}u={{-12}_{⏟}}_{b}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n4q-9=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $q,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4q-9 & =0 \\\\ 4q-9+9 & =0+9 \\\\ 4q & =9 \\\\ \\frac{4q}{4} & =\\frac{9}{4} \\\\ q & =\\frac{9}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["fb8540a4-f01f-56fa-9999-4f7e33a5d3ea"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "generator" :question-generator/id #uuid "b2b16748-3249-59b8-8679-78daaba7b541" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186204092.py"} [:db/add 17592186204092 :knowledge-point/question-generator "generator"] {:db/id 17592186204092 :knowledge-point/questions ["8f4b8651-2348-5ff7-936e-cae0fa3ecd4e" "477ddd4a-3429-5a77-b6eb-21489edaf35e" "1eca6787-bc49-5086-8428-52d3acf41f5a" "b0f885fc-0739-508a-bfee-6d9f76213a02" "d7b7776b-e31d-5294-a559-386b1ec0c77e"]} [:db/ensure 17592186204092 :knowledge-point/validate]]
